{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791049174,"nonce":"+XnrnjlizJi1OJTHMqH9N+36NpM=","title":"Text: upload only what changed in the glyph atlas, subpixel positioning, letter spacing in measurement","message":"Left over from the text and input phase (e532fc0):\n\n- Glyph atlas uploads: the whole atlas is uploaded whenever its revision changes, because blinc_text exposes no dirty rect. Ask Blinc for the rect added since a revision (or track it in blinc_abi), and upload that region only.\n- Subpixel positioning: glyph quads are snapped to whole device pixels when nothing rotates or skews them; horizontal subpixel offsets (e.g. three or four phases per glyph in the atlas) would make text spacing even at small sizes.\n- Letter spacing in measurement: check that a text node's letter spacing (tracking- classes, Prop.LetterSpacing) reaches the measurer as well as the renderer, so a tracked line is laid out as wide as it is drawn; text::tests::layout_measures_text_as_drawn could take a letter-spaced case.","files":null}]}